# v1.23.5 — cache policy. THE chronic "live lags the zip" fix: pages must
# REVALIDATE on every open (no-cache = cheap 304 when unchanged, fresh HTML
# the moment a deploy lands), while hashed build files never need rechecking.
# Without this, phones held old builds long after every DEPLOY.bat.
#
# v1.26.3 (CEO: "I still encounter location for the android phone"): the
# Permissions-Policy below WAS the Android mystery. geolocation=() told
# browsers to forbid the Geolocation API for the whole site — Android
# Chrome/Samsung Internet enforce it (instant "denied" no matter what the
# user allows), while iPhone Safari ignores this directive, which is why
# only Androids were "blocked". It shipped with this very file in v1.23.5 —
# exactly when the Android complaints began. geolocation=(self): our own
# pages may ask; embedded third-party frames still cannot. Camera/mic stay
# locked (nothing in the system uses them).
# NOTE: comments live ONLY here at the top — a # line inside a rule block
# can be misparsed as a header. tests/permissions-policy.mjs guards this.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(self)
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
